## Phase 1 — keymap table completion (auditA #8a)
- table.rs: +44 v2 entries (the 53-entry backlog minus SURF-2's 9
  diff-family additions): app.clear ctrl+l; app.debug/app.scrap/
  opencode.settings/server.pair/service.restart/location.reload
  "none"; pane.focus.left/right <leader>arrows; terminal.select/
  toggle/close <leader>down/t/up; session.copy.id, session.aside,
  session.cd, session.toggle.exploration_grouping,
  session.verbosity.cycle "none"; session.tab.history.back "none" /
  forward ctrl+i; queued_prompt.undo ctrl+u (dialog layer);
  composer.terminal.up up,k / down down,j / select return (composer
  layer); dialog.integration.rename ctrl+r / delete ctrl+d;
  dialog.plugins.error space / install shift+i / update ctrl+u /
  check ctrl+r; plugins.list/plugins.install "none"; which-key ×12
  (ctrl+alt+k family, base — v2 ships the ids without a component
  consumer too).
- Renamed dialog.project_copy.generate → dialog.worktree.generate
  (v2's table id, keybind.ts:267 — auditA's id divergence).
- Removed the DUPLICATE dialog.mcp.toggle row (two bind names, one
  command — the new coverage test's first catch).
- Dispatchers: tab history back/forward (store walks the recorded
  TabHistory cursor, stack preserved across the navigate);
  queued_prompt.undo (removes the LAST queued prompt, miss → error
  toast); session.copy.id (OSC-52 clipboard + info toast);
  session.cd (WorkingDirectory select); session.toggle.
  exploration_grouping (new store signal, wired into the transcript
  walk's group_exploration); plugins.list (DialogKind::Plugins
  select — registered plugin ids, enable state not modeled);
  app.clear + the surfaceless families (terminal/pane/which-key/
  scrap/debug/restart/aside/verbosity/plugins.install/integration/
  plugin-dialog/composer.terminal) → consumed Handled no-ops (v2's
  keymap eats the stroke with no handler either).
- toast.activate PORT ADDITION (ctrl+alt+t, palette Prompt): v2's
  toast action is pointer-only; the port reaches it from the input
  layer (auditA #10's keyboard half). ToastOptions gained
  action_command (v2's action.run → the dot command) and modal (the
  F11 gate narrowed to the Session-failed/send-failure surfaces —
  v2 toasts never block typing; the new MCP-failure toasts stay
  transparent).
- set_mcp_servers now produces v2's toast-once alerts (app.tsx:
  522-545): failed/needs_auth transitions, per-server dedup, action
  "Open MCP servers" → mcp.list.
- parity_tests: table_covers_the_full_v2_default_table — the
  generated 242-entry v2 corpus (keybind.ts Definitions) + leader:
  id+default equality both directions, duplicates by (id, layer),
  registered divergences (app.exit decollision) and port additions
  (heap_snapshot, composer layer commands, diff-layer app.exit,
  toast.activate). The resolution-parity test grew with the table
  (>190 spec cases) — every new binding resolves on BOTH engines.
